# ─── Environment ───
# `.env*` rather than a list, with .env.example negated back in. The list form
# ignored `.env` and `.env.local` but NOT `.env.bak` — and copying .env aside
# before editing it is the most natural thing in the world to do.
.env*
!.env.example

# ─── Node / Bun ───
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── SQLite ───
data/*
!data/README.md
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# ─── Deployment ───
.deployment-state

# ─── Dev Runtime ───
.dev*.pid

# ─── Worktrees ───
# Each `make worktree` nests a parallel checkout here. The leading dot does real work:
# Bun's test discovery and TypeScript's default include both skip hidden directories, so
# the main checkout's `bun test` and root tsconfig never wander into a worktree.
.worktrees/

# ─── IDE ───
.vscode/
.idea/
# Sublime project and workspace files stay local, like the editor folders above. A
# project file describes how one person lays out this checkout beside its sibling
# repositories, which differs between machines, and the workspace file is per-user
# UI state (open tabs, find history, unsaved buffers) that Sublime rewrites constantly.
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── OS ───
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Coverage / Testing ───
coverage/
*.lcov

# ─── Local content storage (dev) ───
/content/

# ─── Dropped web builds (dev) ───
# The dev-only build harness serves from here (apps/web/serve.ts → /dev/web-build). A build
# a developer drops in to test is theirs, not the repo's.
/builds/

# ─── Playwright / browser testing ───
.screenshots/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
# Signed-in storage state the gauntlet setup project mints (session cookie)
.auth/

# ─── Claude Code ───
# Repo slash commands (.claude/commands/) are tracked; personal settings are not
.claude/settings.local.json
# Snapshots/console logs an agent's Tier 1 MCP browser drops here
.playwright-mcp/

# ─── Legacy (Python) ───
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.venv/
venv/
_legacy/backend/staticfiles/

# Agent instructions and per-agent config. Kept local: they point into a private
# working wiki, so on a public repo they are dangling references rather than
# provenance. `.mcp.json` is deliberately NOT here — it registers the Playwright
# MCP server, which is testing tooling that belongs with the repo.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
